  {
   "id": "bIbNiCCTAQAJ",
   "from": "Jenni Poutanen",
   "author": "68d5f085a403524f",
   "date": "2017-11-29T13:48:52Z",
   "subject": "VS: Modelling behavioral response",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;background-color:#ffffff;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">\r\n<p>Hi,</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>Thanks for your replies. </p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>Yes we don&#39;t have recaptures at the same trap. In this dataset we used non-invasive DNA sampling, which should also minimize the behavioral response. But we have also data with trail cameras, which could cause some behavioral effect (this species seem to\r\n be very interested in cameras so they might have an attractive effect). So good to know why the effect couldn&#39;t be modelled here, if the same problem occurs with another dataset.<br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>best regards,<br>\r\nJenni</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font style=\"font-size:11pt\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><b>Lähettäjä:</b> Daniel Linden &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">danl...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Lähetetty:</b> 22. marraskuuta 2017 20:10<br>\r\n<b>Vastaanottaja:</b> Jenni Poutanen<br>\r\n<b>Kopio:</b> oSCR<br>\r\n<b>Aihe:</b> Re: Modelling behavioral response</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;background-color:#ffffff;font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33)\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>Hi Jenni,<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\nThe p.behav coefficient is for a trap-specific behavioral response, so the model is indicating that capture probability essentially goes to zero for a given individual at a given trap after initial capture.  The problem is that you did not observe an individual\r\n recaptured in the same trap.  I&#39;m not sure there is a great fix for this.  If the behavioral response is real, you&#39;d want to keep it in the model to adjust p0 (and subsequently, d0).  But the coefficient will have a nonsense estimate because of the link scale\r\n conversion of Pr(y = 1) = 0, which is negative infinity.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\nWhat kind of traps were used?  If they were live-capture traps, you&#39;d want to make sure the multinomial model (<span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">multicatch = T</span>) is used.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Nov 22, 2017 at 8:33 AM, Jenni Poutanen <span dir=\"ltr\">\r\n&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jenni.p...@utu.fi</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hi group,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I have an issue concerning modelling behavioral response with my white-tailed deer encounter history data.\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">My edf and tdf files are attached here. I have 27 individuals and 7 of them have been recaptured. There are three sampling occasions in the dataset.\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I tried to model behavior (D~1,p0~b,sig~1), but got the following error message:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\" lang=\"EN-US\">In sqrt(diag(solve(myfit$hessian))) : NaNs produced</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\" lang=\"SV\">&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\" lang=\"SV\">mb</span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\"> Model:<span>  </span>D ~ 1 p0 ~ b sig ~ 1</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\">Run time:<span>  </span>8.027167<span>  </span>minutes</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"> AIC:<span>  </span>341.5535</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\">Summary table: </span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>                </span></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">Estimate<span>    </span>SE<span>      </span>z P(&gt;|z|)</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\">p0.(Intercept)<span>    </span>-1.825 0.493 -3.700<span>   </span>0.000</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\">p.behav<span>          </span>-20.998<span>   </span>NaN<span>    </span>NaN<span>     </span>NaN</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\">sig.(Intercept)<span>    </span>5.142 0.163 31.634<span>   </span>0.000</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\">d0.(Intercept)<span>    </span>-2.069 0.275 -7.527<span>   </span>0.000</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"SV\">psi.constant<span>       </span>0.223 0.387<span>  </span>0.576<span>   </span>0.565</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\">*Density intercept is log(individuals per pixel) </span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>  </span>Nhat(state-space) = exp(d0.)*nrow(ssDF)</span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:10.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>  </span>(caution is warranted when model contains density covariates)</span></pre>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">So does this mean that this can&#39;t be run? And if so, why is this?\r\n<br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thanks for your time,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><br>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Jenni Poutanen</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">PhD student</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Section of Ecology</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Biology Department</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">University of Turku, Finland</span></p>\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"></font></span></div>\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;oSCR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_package+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">\r\noscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/e2b8a270-2d08-4dc9-9516-4e1360b061a4%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/e2b8a270-2d08-4dc9-9516-4e1360b061a4%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492254858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DnXgYN89gqoexuJ_l9fK5\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/e2b8a270-2d08-4dc9-9516-4e1360b061a4%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492254858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CJHt0eyermBrYRs6vMiQm\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
